<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.005 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.005 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.2 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due August 28, 1997 was 3.005 percent, down from 3.114 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 175-day T-bills due November 20, 1997 was 3.392 percent, down from 3.462 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due May 28, 1998 was 3.868 percent, down from 3.892 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$500 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$950 million of C$5.8 billion bills due May 5.  </p>
